ASTEROID, BENNU -- asteroid-bennu.jpg -- 2400 x 1200
Credit: NASA/Goddard/University of Arizona.
Official mission source: https://osiris-rex.lpl.arizona.edu/bennu_global_mosaic/
NASA visualization context: https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5069/
Download: https://osiris-rex.lpl.arizona.edu/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/Bennu_Global_Mosaic.png
Downloaded PNG SHA-256: 648e2469f71e533a7f963bd32d83027c86024158f58a482465dbbd183d37e0bf
OSIRIS-REx OCAMS/PolyCam images acquired 7 March to 19 April 2019.
Citation: Bennett, C. A., et al. (2020), A high-resolution global Basemap of
(101955) Bennu, Icarus. Publication linked from the official mission source.
Processing: the mission's 2400 x 1200 presentation PNG was encoded as RGB JPEG
(Pillow, quality 95, subsampling 0), with no crop, resize or colour adjustment.
No generative AI is used. This is a reduced global mosaic of spacecraft images,
not generic asteroid artwork. The source mosaic retains shadows and polar
lighting differences. The viewer maps it onto its existing sphere; it does not
reproduce Bennu's irregular shape or turn the selected simulation into a Bennu
model. The saved-view identifier 'planetesimal' is retained for compatibility.
